A||N||3||stimpy||Cold start issues + lagging in 2nd gear.||||5||
Z||000000||stimpy||05-01-2001||12:41 PM||||Well, here's the scoop. Lately, whenever I start the car after it has set for at least 8 hours, it will fluctuate wildly between 1500 and 700 rpm. It sounds like it wants to stall out. After it runs for a couple of minutes, it locks in the idle right around 1100 rpm. When I drive away, it powers through 1st gear ok (although it seems a little lagging off the line) but when I get into second, it hesitates through 2500-3500 rpm.<P>I've recently replaced O2 sensor, alternator, and battery. EGR tube replaced 2 years ago. The cat is less then 4 yrs old and the engine has only 11000 miles on it. Oil level and pressure is good. What should I be checking for now? What's a good way to check for vacuum leaks? <P>Help me Mr. Wizard!||||reg||5
Z||000001||thomas_l||05-01-2001||12:56 PM||||TPS could have a dead spot - that would cause both the idle changes and hesitation. Put a DVOM on it and slooowly move the throttle thru its travel to see if it has any "dips" in voltage. It should smoothly increase from the minimum (not sure - a little less than 1V) to the max (around 4.5V). Also check the vacuum lines, especially look at any rubber section that connects to the MAP sensor to dee if has rotted and collapsed.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HummelHund||05-01-2001||04:33 PM||||Check for vaccuum leaks for the idle problem, but for the hesitation thing don't forget to check your timing. The timing on my 2M4 was an inch off the scale, I reset it and now it doesn't stumble anymore. I don't know how you set the timing on a V6, though.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||HummelHund||05-01-2001||04:35 PM||||Before I forget, to check for vacuum leaks use an aerosol can of Fuel Injector/Carb Cleaner or WD40 and spray it on all the vaccuum hoses. If there's a hole or split the car should rev up some.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
